  <title>2.4.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00431</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.4.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>12a977a8-94a8-4de6-ade6-9255e984ac83</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<para>For questions 1 – 8, solve the systems of equations using the elimination method.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="de4b55db-3c3d-4fbf-802a-2fdb361502fa"><problem><para>
      <para> \(\begin{array}{c}\left\{\begin{array}{l}5x\;+\;2y\;=\;2\\-6x\;-\;2y\;=\;0\end{array}\right.\\\\\end{array}\)</para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((–3,9)\)</para><para>\((0,1)\)</para><para>\((2,–4)\)</para><para>\((–2,6)\)</para></problem><solution><para>\((–2,6)\)</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is (–2,6). </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section>
<para>For questions 9 – 10, add the equations in the following systems of equations. What is the resulting new equation?</para>

<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="15b8e870-9833-4088-8cc6-2900e1100eaf"><problem><para>
      <para> \(\begin{array}{c}\left\{\begin{array}{l}4x\;-\;6y\;=\;14\\-4x\;+\;y\;=\;-19\end{array}\right.\\\\\end{array}\)</para>
      </para></problem><solution><para>-5y = -5</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \(–5y = –5\). </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
